# Captured from vanilla 26.2 (protocol 776) survival oracle.
# Packet: clientbound container_set_slot, from
# `item replace entity <player> weapon.mainhand with minecraft:diamond_pickaxe`.
#
# ..        VarInt window id  (session-scoped; not compared)
# ..        VarInt state id   (container revision; not compared)
# ..        i16    slot index (not compared)
# 01        VarInt stack count = 1
# c6 07     VarInt item registry id 966 = minecraft:diamond_pickaxe
# 00        DataComponentPatch: 0 added
# 00        DataComponentPatch: 0 removed
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE: those last two bytes are the whole patch.
# A real diamond pickaxe sends NO minecraft:tool. The component lives in
# the item's prototype component map (ToolMaterial.applyToolProperties),
# and a clientbound stack transmits only the delta from that prototype,
# so the client is expected to already know it. Decoding the wire alone
# can never make a pickaxe dig faster; the per-item census in
# src/generated/tools.rs is what does.
00 02 00 24 01 c6 07 00 00
